	json('{"en":{"title":"Opus-Fable Video Pro: 7 skills for animated 4K videos with Claude","tagline":"Claude designs, animates, scores it and hands you the finished MP4","summary":"Seven skills for Claude: titles, explainers, 2.5D landscapes, 3D action and ads. Claude writes the video in code and delivers a 30 fps MP4 in 4K (or 2K).","meta_title":"Opus-Fable Video Pro: animated videos with Claude in 4K","meta_description":"Make animated videos with Claude: 7 skills for titles, explainers, landscapes, 3D action and ads. Claude writes them in code and delivers a 4K MP4.","description":"Need an intro for your channel, an explainer with maps and data or a short ad, without animating by hand or hiring a studio? Opus-Fable Video Pro is a pack of seven skills for Claude. With them, Claude produces finished videos by writing code: it designs the look, animates it, composes the music and sound effects, reviews its own work and delivers an MP4 ready to publish, at 30 fps in 4K (or 2K when your machine can''t handle 4K). You don''t need to know animation or coding: you describe what you want, attach what is needed and Claude follows the skill''s process from start to finish.\n\nInside the ZIP the pack is called Code Video Studio V3: that is the name you will see in the LEEME-PRIMERO (read me first) guide, in the README and in the files. It is the same product.\n\nOpus-Fable Video Pro is an independent product by Tony Ciencia: it works with Claude, but it is not an official Anthropic product and it is not endorsed by Anthropic. Opus and Fable are names of Claude models.\n\n## The problem it solves\n\nAn animated video has many parts: design, animation, music, effects, timing and a render that doesn''t fail. These skills give Claude the whole process: research, design, show you a style frame, make a draft, review it and render the final. Before animating it shows you a still with the final look, the cheapest moment to change course, and at the end a check reviews resolution, fps, duration, loudness and motion.\n\n## The 7 skills\n\n- title-sequence: series openers, channel intros, reels and brand bumpers, with original music.\n- editorial-collage-explainer: explainer videos for a narration, in paper collage with real maps and data, from 20 seconds to several minutes.\n- parallax-landscape-animation: mood scenes with depth, a directed camera, something that grows or changes, and composed music.\n- character-explainer-animation: an explanation told by characters in an illustrated world, synced to the narration.\n- action-scene-3d: 3D fights, duels and chases from one sheet per character.\n- product-spot: 6- to 30-second ads, with a recomposed vertical version for social media.\n- video-director: takes a loose request (\"make me a video for…\"), picks the right skill, writes the brief, reviews the style frame and the delivery, and assembles the final package. It needs the other six installed.\n\n## How it works, in 5 steps\n\n- Choose what to make, or ask video-director and let it choose.\n- Prepare what is needed: a narration MP3 or WAV for the explainers, one sheet per character for 3D, or name, promise and tagline for a spot. Title sequences and landscapes need nothing.\n- Copy one of the tested briefs in docs/PROMPTS.md (there is one for every skill, in English and Spanish) and change your details.\n- Approve the style frame.\n- Review the delivery. Don''t accept it until the check says PASS.\n\n## What you get\n\n- The 7 skills, one per .skill file, for Claude Code or to upload in claude.ai.\n- docs/PROMPTS.md with every brief in English and Spanish, the README and LICENSES (third-party components and their licenses).\n- extras/: scripts and narrations of the demos, the sheets of the characters Ori and Gor and the illustrations of the long explainer, so you can reproduce them.\n- The LEEME-PRIMERO guide as a PDF (English and Spanish): installation, your first video, how to ask for what you want and common problems.\n- With every video you make: final.mp4 (4K or 2K master, 30 fps, with sound), a 1080p preview, a poster, a contact sheet of 12 frames, notes.md (chosen style, fonts and data with their licenses, what was checked and what fell short) and verify.txt.\n\n## Who it is for\n\nCreators and brands that need openers, channel intros, explainers, mood scenes or short ads, and would rather have Claude make them in code than animate by hand or hire a studio.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Claude, with your own account (not included). Recommended: Claude Code, where the skills were built and tested. In claude.ai or the desktop app they are used with code execution turned on, but they have not been tested there on long 4K pieces: run a short test first. On Enterprise plans, an admin must enable skills and code execution.\n- Node.js 18 or later with Playwright and Chromium, Python 3 with numpy and ffmpeg; faster-whisper for narrated pieces and three.js for 3D. If something is missing, Claude installs it with your permission.\n- About 2.5 GB of free memory per 4K render process.\n- Windows, macOS or Linux. No graphics card needed.\n\n## Important\n\n- In the pack''s tests, on a 2-core machine without a graphics card, a complete piece took from 30 minutes to 2 hours and the final render of 30 seconds in 4K about 20 minutes. Each piece used from 150,000 to 400,000 tokens: if your plan has usage limits, count on one or two pieces per session.\n- 4K is not guaranteed: if the pre-render measurement shows it would take too long, it comes out in 2K. 3D pieces are rendered in software and come out in 2K; with a graphics card they can come out in 4K.\n- Claude measures the loudness of the sound, but it cannot hear it: listen to each video before publishing and, if needed, ask it to remaster to −14 LUFS.\n- The demo videos in the images are not in the ZIP; their scripts, narrations and sheets are.\n- Generated images are optional: it uses your image connector in Claude or your own Google AI Studio key (GEMINI_API_KEY, not included). Without either, Claude draws the illustrations in code.\n- The skills ask for original content: they don''t reproduce existing logos, characters or works, and they record in notes.md the fonts and data they use, all openly licensed. Anything you add (logos, images, music) is your responsibility.\n- This is version 3.","highlights":["7 skills: titles, editorial and character explainers, 2.5D landscapes, 3D action, ads and a director","Claude designs, animates, composes the music and effects, reviews its work and delivers the MP4","30 fps MP4 in 4K (2K if your machine can''t handle 4K), in 16:9, 9:16 or both","You approve a style frame before animating, and the delivery only counts when verify.txt says PASS","Tested briefs for every skill, in English and Spanish, ready to copy","Every delivery comes with a 1080p preview, poster, contact sheet and notes on fonts and licenses"],"specs":[{"label":"Version","value":"3 (Code Video Studio V3 inside the ZIP)"},{"label":"Format","value":"ZIP with 7 skills (.skill), briefs, README, licenses, demo extras and the LEEME-PRIMERO guide as a PDF"},{"label":"Works with","value":"Claude with your account (not included): Claude Code recommended, or claude.ai and the desktop app with code execution"},{"label":"Requirements","value":"Node.js 18+ with Playwright and Chromium, Python 3 with numpy and ffmpeg; faster-whisper (narration) and three.js (3D); about 2.5 GB free per 4K render"},{"label":"Systems","value":"Windows, macOS and Linux, no graphics card needed (3D comes out in 2K)"},{"label":"Output","value":"30 fps MP4 with sound, in 4K or 2K, 16:9, 9:16 or both; 1080p preview, poster, contact sheet, notes.md and verify.txt"},{"label":"Language","value":"Guide and briefs in English and Spanish"},{"label":"License","value":"1 user: use it in your business or in client projects; the pack can''t be resold or redistributed"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is this an official Anthropic product?","a":"No. Opus-Fable Video Pro is an independent product by Tony Ciencia that works with Claude. It is not made by Anthropic and it is not endorsed by Anthropic. Opus and Fable are names of Claude models, by Anthropic."},{"q":"Why does the ZIP say Code Video Studio V3?","a":"Opus-Fable Video Pro is the name in the store; inside, the pack is called Code Video Studio V3. That is the name you will see in the LEEME-PRIMERO guide, in the README and in the files. It is the same product, version 3."},{"q":"Do I need to know animation or coding?","a":"No. You describe what you want, attach what is needed (a narration or a character sheet) and Claude follows the skill''s process. To install them you copy the skills into your skills folder (or upload them in claude.ai), and if a program is missing, Claude installs it with your permission."},{"q":"How long does each video take and how many tokens does it use?","a":"In the pack''s tests, on a 2-core machine without a graphics card, a complete piece took from 30 minutes to 2 hours and used from 150,000 to 400,000 tokens. If your Claude plan has usage limits, count on one or two pieces per session."},{"q":"Does it work in claude.ai or only in Claude Code?","a":"Claude Code is recommended: rendering means running commands and working for several minutes in a row, and the skills were tested there. In claude.ai or the desktop app they load with code execution turned on, but they have not been tested on long 4K pieces: run a short test first."},{"q":"Do I need a graphics card?","a":"No. The times in the guide were measured without a graphics card. Without one, 3D pieces come out in 2K; with a graphics card they can come out in 4K."},{"q":"Can I use the videos in my business or for clients?","a":"The license lets you use the product in your own business or in your clients'' projects; what you can''t do is resell or redistribute the pack. The skills ask for original content and record in notes.md the fonts and data they use, all openly licensed. Anything you add (logos, images, music) is your responsibility, and if you use images generated with your Google key, check that service''s terms."},{"q":"Are the demo videos included?","a":"No: the videos in the images were made with these skills, but they are not in the ZIP. Their scripts, narrations, the Ori and Gor sheets and the illustrations of the long explainer are included, so you can reproduce them."}],"tags":["animated videos with Claude","Claude skills for video","AI video made in code","animated YouTube intros","AI animated explainers","AI video ads","4K videos with Claude Code"],"image_alts":["Opus-Fable Video Pro: real frames from three demos made with the skills (titles, 2.5D landscape and character explainer)","The 7 skills of Opus-Fable Video Pro, with real frames from the title, editorial collage, landscape and character demos","How Opus-Fable Video Pro works: 5 steps, the files in every delivery and what your machine needs"]}}')
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM products WHERE slug = 'opus-fable-video-pro');
